  "note": "Platform-neutral key intents of the pin scripts (widget survey §5.2), resolved per platform. Chords are X keysym names joined with +; Cmd is the macOS command key. A step with \"shift\": true adds Shift. Pins 4-6 (WG3b): redo is the platform chord, redo-alt the other common one (no second chord on macOS); copy-alt, cut-alt and paste-alt are the IBM CUA chords (Linux and Windows); dead keys are X keysyms (Windows: the US-International layout; macOS: Option chords); unicode-entry is GTK's and IBus's Ctrl+Shift+U (Linux only).",
